<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand VII of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a>–<a href="/years/1833">1833</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand VII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1808 and again from 1813 to 1833. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> forced him and his father Charles IV to abdicate at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonne">Bayonne</a> in 1808 and held him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, while juntas in Spain and America governed in his name. Restored in 1814, he abolished the liberal Constitution of 1812 and ruled as an absolute monarch as the American colonies won independence. His Pragmatic Sanction in favour of his daughter Isabella led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlist-wars">Carlist Wars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-vii-of-spain.jpg" alt="Ferdinand VII of Spain" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vicente López Portaña · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fernando_VII_-_Vicente_L%C3%B3pez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
